- `unit-tests`: `BerremanTests.MuellerInverseTests`

**How to implement.** Layer 2 reuses the study engine's own algebra (the S14.2 brief: 'REUSING the study engine's OWN forward model and FitQuality.residualJacobian / MuellerInverse.ResidualJacobian'; 001 §M 'the study engine's own forward model and Jacobian, REUSED'), so four rules it needs become callable where they live. Each is a MOVE (.spec-md §4 'A reuse is a move or a call: the new home is created and the old body deleted in the same step'; AGENTS.md 'Reuse, never copy'): after the step each rule has one body, and every number BerremanTests and the study engine compute is unchanged. Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S14.2. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Optimization/FitQuality.fs`: the private `covarianceMatrix` (`FitQuality.fs:covarianceMatrix`, Cov = reducedχ² · (JᵀJ)⁻¹ through the `RealMatrix` seam) becomes the public `covarianceOf (jacobian : ResidualJacobian) (reduced : ReducedChiSquared) : ParameterMatrix`, its body unchanged, and `reportFrom` (`FitQuality.fs:reportFrom`) calls it; its doc keeps the line naming the `MathNetNumericsMath` seam. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Optimization/FittedProblems.fs` (step 397): the offset frame that `FittedProblem.jacobian` and `FittedProblem.report` both evaluate (the residual y ↦ residual (start + y − 100), taken at the vector holding 100 in every coordinate, so FitQuality's relative step is about 1.5e-6 in the solve's own coordinates and a coordinate at zero is still perturbed) MOVES, before `FittedProblem`, into `type ScaledVector with` (`MuellerInverse.fs:ScaledVector`) `member this.offsetResidualOf (residual : ScaledVector -> ResidualVector) : Residual` (`OptimizationInterface.fs:Residual`), that closure about this point; `member this.offsetOrigin : DesignVector`, the vector of hundreds of this point's length; and `member this.offsetJacobianOf (residual : ScaledVector -> ResidualVector) : ResidualJacobian`, `FitQuality.residualJacobian (this.offsetResidualOf residual) this.offsetOrigin` (`FitQuality.fs:residualJacobian`), whose doc keeps step 397's one line on why the frame is offset. `jacobian` becomes `this.search.start.offsetJacobianOf this.residual`, and `report` becomes `FitQuality.reportFrom (this.search.start.offsetResidualOf this.residual) this.search.start.offsetOrigin (this.residual this.search.start)`, so the same doubles flow. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Optimization/BenchNoise.fs` (step 339): the angle shift `disturb` applies (`InverseFitHarness.fs:disturb`: the incidence through the engine's `IncidenceAngle + Angle` operator, the azimuth through `SampleAzimuth`) MOVES into `type MeasurementConfiguration with member this.misalignedBy (incidence : Angle) (azimuth : Angle) : MeasurementConfiguration` (`MuellerInverse.fs:MeasurementConfiguration`), declared before `disturb`, its doc keeping in one line why the operator and not `IncidenceAngle.create` carries a signed excursion; `disturb` becomes `c.misalignedBy (wobble ()) (wobble ())`. F# evaluates the two arguments left to right, so the incidence draw still comes first and every seeded experiment is bit-identical. (4) `OpticalConstructor.Optimization/StudyEngine.fs` (step 387): the per-entry unit `scaledProblemWith` computes (the bounds' span over twice `studySearchBox.halfWidth`) MOVES into `type ParameterInterval with member this.searchUnit : ParameterValue` (`ParameterInterval`, S7.1 step 214), declared directly after `studySearchBox`, and `scaledProblemWith` calls it. Every consumer opens the module where the compiler asks and changes nothing else. No other declaration of the four files changes, no test is removed, and the fit, profile, noise and study numbers are unchanged: `MuellerInverseTests` reaches `reportFrom` through `MuellerFitData.report` and `disturb` through its noisy facts, and AT-1 and AT-2 reach `FittedProblem`, `scaledProblemWith` and the bench through their study fits and AT-2's data. Tests: `FitResultsTests` (step 397) gains `the offset frame differentiates a residual about any point, zero included, and covarianceOf scales the inverse normal matrix`: for the linear residual r(x) = A x − b with A = [[1; 2]; [0; 1]; [3; 0]], `(ScaledVector [| 0.0; 0.0 |]).offsetJacobianOf` answers A and so does `(ScaledVector [| 5.0; −3.0 |]).offsetJacobianOf`, with b = 0, each entry within 1e-6 (forward differences at a step of about 1.5e-6), and `FitQuality.covarianceOf (ResidualJacobian A) (ReducedChiSquared 0.5)` is 0.5 · (AᵀA)⁻¹ written out in the test ((AᵀA) = [[10; 2]; [2; 5]]), within 1e-12. `StudyEngineTests` (step 381) gains `an interval's search unit is its span over twice the search box's half-width`: `{ lower = ParameterValue 1.0; upper = ParameterValue 2.0 }.searchUnit` is `ParameterValue 0.01` (a span of 1 over 2 · 50) within 1e-15.

**Acceptance.** After the moves, `FitQuality.covarianceOf`, `ScaledVector.offsetResidualOf`, `offsetOrigin` and `offsetJacobianOf`, `MeasurementConfiguration.misalignedBy` and `ParameterInterval.searchUnit` MUST each hold the one body of the rule it names, called by `reportFrom`, `FittedProblem.jacobian` and `report`, `disturb` and `scaledProblemWith`; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `the offset frame differentiates a residual about any point, zero included, and covarianceOf scales the inverse normal matrix` and `an interval's search unit is its span over twice the search box's half-width`, the count rising by 2; unit-tests MUST pass over the selected class `BerremanTests.MuellerInverseTests`, its numbers and count unchanged; kit-acceptance MUST pass over `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitAcceptanceTests`, its count unchanged; and build, elevation and the twenty-one s46 invariants MUST pass.
